<title>MOROCCO: Moroccan Treasury auction raises 260 mln dirhams.</title>
<headline>Moroccan Treasury auction raises 260 mln dirhams.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Moroccan Treasury raised 260 million dirhams from its weekly treasury bill auction, Bank al-Maghrib (central bank) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Rates were unchanged, and amounts (in million dirhams) which were accepted:</p>
<p>    MATURITY	BID	 AMOUNT		INTEREST RATE</p>
<p>    26 weeks	 5.0	 not allocated	 8.5  pct</p>
<p>    52 weeks	 5.0	 not allocaled	 9.0  pct</p>
<p>    Two years     20	   not allocated	 9.5  pct</p>
<p>    10 years	15	   15		     10.25 pct</p>
<p>    15 years	245	 245		     10.50 percent</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    Total	  290	  260</p>
<p>The next auction will be on December 3, the bank said.</p>
<p>($1= 8.7 dirhams)</p>
<p>- Rabat newsroom +212-7 726518</p>
</text>
